#  문체: 단독 저자 무인칭(we 금지), 미국식 철자. 다른 호 원고는 인용·언급하지 않음.
def intro(N):
    return [
 ("Seasonal influenza causes substantial morbidity and mortality in older adults, and annual vaccination is considered the most important preventive intervention in this group [@nagata2013social]. "
  "Korea provides free influenza vaccination through its National Immunization Program to adults aged 65 years or older and, after expansions in the late 2010s, to children and pregnant women; coverage is high in these groups but much lower among adults outside the free program, including many with chronic diseases [@seo2022impact]. "
  "National coverage among adults rose through the 2010s [@yang2014influenza; @kim2025national] and changed again during the COVID-19 pandemic, with different responses across income, education, and age groups [@kim2025national; @kim2024influenza; @lee2025effect; @yeo2025socioeconomic]."),
 ("Vaccination coverage also differs between places. In England, neighborhood deprivation was associated with lower uptake among older adults and young children, and some neighborhoods departed from what their deprivation would predict [@hungerford2018influenza; @green2026learning]. "
  "In the United States, county social vulnerability was associated with lower coverage among Medicare beneficiaries, with associations that varied across regions [@strully2022county]. "
  "In Australia, by contrast, childhood vaccination was lowest in the most socioeconomically advantaged areas, a pattern described as a privilege paradox [@bryden2019privilege]. "
  "Small-area models that combine survey estimates with spatial smoothing have been used to map vaccination coverage for local planning [@jia2006monitoring; @seeskin2024estimating; @utazi2021district]."),
 ("A social-ecological view of health behavior holds that preventive behaviors share individual, community, and service-level determinants and therefore tend to cluster. "
  "In the KCHS, older age, lower education and income, regular walking, and receiving health check-ups were associated with influenza vaccination, whereas smoking and drinking were inversely associated [@yang2014influenza]; in the Korea National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey, current smokers were less often vaccinated [@park2018association]. "
  "In the United States, regular physical activity was associated with vaccination uptake [@tian2019characteristics], although few adults met recommendations for vaccination, sleep, and physical activity at the same time [@webber2023joint]. "
  "Vaccinated older adults are also on average healthier than unvaccinated ones, a pattern known as the healthy-user effect [@jackson2006evidence]. "
  "Socioeconomic gradients in vaccination differ between countries and depend on whether vaccination is free for target groups [@nagata2013social; @jemna2024socio; @zanobini2022health]."),
 ("The geography of adult influenza vaccination across all Korean districts does not appear to have been modeled over time, and it is unknown whether district differences in vaccination follow district differences in other health behaviors. "
  "This study therefore asked three questions. First, does age-sex-standardized adult influenza vaccination coverage cluster among the 229 Korean districts, and are district ranks stable over 14 years? "
  "Second, are district physical activity, sports facilities, education, welfare receipt, and household composition associated with district vaccination coverage after structural controls? "
  "Third, are these associations robust to model specification, space-time interaction, spatial confounding, and the fact that the physical activity indicators come from the same survey as the outcome?"),
    ]
def methods(N, NSPEC):
    return [
 ("Design and data",
  ("This was an ecological panel study of all 229 Korean municipal districts (si, gun, and gu) from 2011 to 2024. The outcome was the KCHS influenza vaccination rate: the percentage of adults aged 19 years or older who reported receiving an influenza vaccination in the past 12 months "
   "[@kang2015korea; @web:kdca2026kchs]. The Korea Disease Control and Prevention Agency publishes, for each district and year, a rate directly standardized for age and sex to the 2005 projected population, the standard error of that standardized rate, which reflects the complex survey design, and the number of respondents. "
   "Because free vaccination is offered from age 65 years, district differences in the share of older residents would by themselves produce differences in crude coverage; direct standardization removes this age-composition effect, and the crude rate was used only in a sensitivity analysis with an age-65 control. "
   f"Published district estimates were linked by administrative code to the 229 districts used by Statistics Korea. All {N['n_cells']:,} district-years were observed ({N['n_resp_total']:,} responses; median {N['n_resp_median']:,} per district-year)."),
  ("Seven district covariates were selected for the analysis. Walking prevalence (walking at least 30 minutes a day on at least 5 days in the past week) and the prevalence of moderate-or-higher physical activity came from the same KCHS district tables [@web:kdca2026kchs]; the latter was not published for 2018 and was linearly interpolated between adjacent years within districts. "
   "Public sports facilities and village sports facilities per 100,000 residents came from national sports facility registers [@web:mcst2026facilities]. The share of adults with a university degree, the basic livelihood security recipient rate, and the share of single-person households came from Statistics Korea [@web:kosis2026]. "
   "The university-educated share came from the 2010, 2015, and 2020 population and housing censuses, linearly interpolated between census years and carried forward from 2020 for 2021-2024. Recipient rates for 33 district-years in 2021-2023 that were implausibly low because of reporting changes were treated as missing and interpolated within districts. "
   "Single-person household shares, available from 2015, were filled with district means for 2011-2014. Five structural controls entered every model: the urban-zoned population share, clinics per 100,000 residents, the sex ratio, fiscal autonomy (the share of local revenue that the district can spend at its discretion), and the share of residents aged 80 years or older. "
   "All covariates were standardized over all district-years, so odds ratios are expressed per 1 standard deviation (SD). "
   "Directions were specified before model fitting: higher coverage with more walking, physical activity, and sports facilities (clustering of health behaviors and local health-promotion infrastructure), with more university-educated adults (health literacy and use of preventive services), and with more welfare recipients (free vaccination and public health center contact for low-income adults), and lower coverage with more single-person households (fewer social prompts)."),
  ("The same vaccination indicator republished in a second official database was excluded as a covariate. "
   "Three negative-control exposures with no expected direct link to vaccination were included: fires per 10,000 residents, the share of multicultural marriages, and rear-seat belt use."),
 ),
 ("Statistical analysis",
  ("A spatiotemporal Fay-Herriot model was fitted [@fay1979estimates; @mercer2015space]. The logit of each district-year rate p was treated as normally distributed around a linear predictor with known sampling variance (SE/100)<sup>2</sup>/[p(1 − p)]<sup>2</sup>, derived from the published standard error (in percentage points) by the delta method, with the observation precision fixed. "
   "The linear predictor contained the covariates, a BYM2 spatial effect on a 593-edge contiguity graph (islands linked to their nearest mainland district) with penalized-complexity priors (P[σ > 0.5] = 0.01; P[φ < 0.5] = 2/3) [@riebler2016intuitive; @simpson2017penalising], a first-order random walk and an unstructured effect for year, and an unstructured district-year effect for model error. "
   "Fixed effects had Gaussian priors (mean 0, precision 4; intercept precision 0.001), and other random-effect precisions had penalized-complexity priors (P[σ > 0.5] = 0.01). "
   "Models were fitted with integrated nested Laplace approximation in R [@rue2009approximate; @web:rcore2026]. An association was described as credible when its 95% credible interval (CrI) excluded 1."),
  ("Spatial structure was summarized by Moran's I of the 14-year district mean logit rate, the 90th/10th percentile ratio of 14-year district mean rates, the Spearman correlation of district ranks between 2011-2015 and 2020-2024, Kendall's W across years, the BYM2 mixing parameter, and district hotspots and coldspots (posterior probability that the spatial odds ratio exceeded 1 above 0.95 or below 0.05). "
   "Moran's I was tested with 999 permutations, so p = 0.001 is the smallest attainable value. Residual spatial autocorrelation was tested with a two-sided permutation test. "
   "A descriptive decomposition used the variances of the posterior means of the covariate, control, spatial, temporal, and district-year components together with the mean sampling variance."),
  (f"Robustness was assessed in several steps. (1) A multiverse of all {NSPEC} non-empty subsets of the seven covariates, each with the controls [@steegen2016increasing]; a covariate was called robust if its CrI excluded 1 in at least 75% of the models containing it, with at least 95% sign agreement, "
   "and if it remained credible in the Knorr-Held type II (district-specific random walks over time) and type IV (spatially and temporally structured interaction) models; type III (spatially structured interaction varying independently by year) was also fitted [@knorrheld2000bayesian]. The covariate set (all seven covariates) was fixed before fitting, and four smaller sets were compared by WAIC only. "
   "(2) Sensitivity to spatial confounding was assessed with restricted spatial regression (spatial effect constrained to be orthogonal to the district-mean covariates) and Spatial+ (covariates residualized on 23 low-frequency eigenvectors of the graph Laplacian) [@hodges2010adding; @khan2022restricted; @dupont2022spatial]. "
   "(3) Between-district and within-district components were separated by entering district means and annual deviations [@bell2015explaining]. (4) Further checks were calendar windows (2011-2015, 2016-2019, 2020-2024), a post-2020 interaction, exclusion of the pandemic years 2020-2021, 1-year and 2-year lags, leaving out each province, "
   "alternative likelihoods (binomial with effective sample size, beta, unweighted Gaussian, and crude rate with an age-65 control), a queen contiguity graph derived directly from the boundary file, alternative priors, removal of influential district-years (standardized residual above 3), and covariate slopes varying across five regions. "
   "(5) Because walking and moderate-or-higher physical activity were measured in the same survey respondents as vaccination, the main model was refitted without these two covariates and with each added back alone, and survey-operation effects were examined by adding province-by-year random effects and, separately, other KCHS items (diabetic kidney testing alone, or an index that also included rear-seat belt use and nutrition label use). "
   "(6) The share of manufacturing workers, available only from 2017, was added in a 2017-2024 model. Reporting followed STROBE [@vonelm2007strengthening]."),
  ("Associations opposite to the hypothesized direction were examined with additional post hoc models (single-covariate models and models omitting correlated covariates), which are labelled as post hoc. "
   "The institutional review board approved the study and waived informed consent because only published aggregate statistics were used (approval numbers are given on the title page)."),
 ),
    ]
